body:
Cross-project implementation contract: https://github.com/joshyorko/rcc/issues/118

#118 now defines the concrete RCC/Holotree v1 path consumed here:

- cryptographic Environment Artifact Manifest + Object Index layered over existing v12 catalogs/current Hololib bytes;
- explicit separation between legacy SipHash cache keys and remote trust identities;
- provider publication/acquisition with verified objects and atomic manifest commit;
- worker-local materialization, lease, Execution Handle, and GC semantics;
- per-build/per-artifact/per-materialization coordination rather than a fleet-wide Holotree lock;
- source-only autoreload reuse and generation-safe environment-changing reload;
- a first two-process vertical that does not require a new catalog format, zstd, packfiles, FUSE, OCI, a daemon, or Kubernetes.

Treat #118 as the engine-side authority and this issue as the Runtime adapter/consumer contract.

## Implementation split and RCC lineage — 2026-08-18

This issue remains the full Actions environment-substrate contract. The board now has a bounded first implementation and explicit RCC dependencies.

### Immediate Actions child

- #134 — replace current local Action Server path/activation caching with an RCC EnvironmentBackend lifecycle while preserving current v2 package authoring, autoreload, frozen binary operation, and the existing process pool.

#134 is intentionally local/collapsed. It proves the Runtime can keep Environment Artifact/materialization/lease identity authoritative before #90 introduces independent workers.

### RCC program split

- `joshyorko/rcc#120` — release Environment Artifacts v1 / v18.19.0 handoff;
- `joshyorko/rcc#121` — supported-platform and ABI compatibility matrix;
- `joshyorko/rcc#122` — lease/crash/repair/GC semantics;
- `joshyorko/rcc#123` — production provider hardening;
- `joshyorko/rcc#124` — ZIP/bundle/offline/OCI carrier convergence;
- `joshyorko/rcc#125` — evidence-driven materializer/storage selection;
- `joshyorko/rcc#126` — provenance/SBOM/signatures/revocation/trust;
- `joshyorko/rcc#127` — cold-build coordination and prewarm.

Only #120 and the stable local lifecycle surface are prerequisites for the first #134 vertical. Do not block local Actions integration on every RCC follow-up.

### Historical correction

Legacy RCC already enabled same-platform portability through shared mode, Hololib ZIP export/import, and `rccremote` delta pull. The new contract does not invent transfer; it makes the existing capability cryptographically identified, natively publishable, usable from independent private RCC homes, lifecycle-managed through Materialization/Lease/Execution Handle, and schedulable by durable Artifact identity.

### Handoff invariant

Actions may retain Environment Specification/Artifact digests, compatibility policy, trust decision, and provider reference. It must not retain `PYTHON_EXE`, `CONDA_PREFIX`, `ROBOCORP_HOME`, Holotree paths, provider URL, or RCC PID as durable identity.

The old `env-info/<hash>.json` path must have one bounded migration/validation authority, not remain an equal second source of truth indefinitely.
